# Credentials. LPLens itself never reads these — the extension's only key store
# is chrome.storage.local, written by the options page, inside the browser
# profile. .env exists so the packager's leak scan (tools/package.mjs,
# envSecrets) knows what values must never appear in a build or a commit.
.env
.env.*

# Wrangler local state for the licence Worker. Contains request metadata
# including approximate location and ISP.
.wrangler/

# Rebuildable output of `node tools/package.mjs`. A build is a zip of
# extension/; publishing a stale one is exactly what the packager prevents.
build/

# Internal verification write-ups and monetisation planning. Kept local by
# choice, not because they are secret.
docs/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
node_modules/
*.sync-conflict-*
